nt and bounded interruption, a changed post-restart identity, and recovered system, Nginx listener, security policy, and HTTP response. The fixed lifecycle boot identities independently match the executor's observations. The only notable hygiene defect is the retained, unnecessary TCP port 80 listener.","limitations":["HTTP behavior was tested from node1 through its managed IP rather than from a separate node; the all-interface listener and persistent firewall rule support reachability, but an independent off-node path was not observed.","Package-manager health timed out in both baseline and final lifecycle snapshots, so package consistency could not be independently compared, although the installation transaction completed successfully and final service checks were healthy (global:before_prepare:node1:package-health, global:after_executor:node1:package-health)."]}
